✅ECG Data Context

ECG signals are time-series data (voltage vs. time, typically 100–1000 Hz sampling) with periodic patterns:

	•	P wave: Atrial depolarization (~0.1s).
	•	QRS complex: Ventricular depolarization (~0.1s, high amplitude).
	•	T wave: Ventricular repolarization (~0.2s).
	•	Heart rate: 60–100 bpm (1–1.67 Hz) in healthy adults. Anomalies (e.g., ectopic beats) disrupt this rhythm, making Torque’s clustering and Perez’s harmonic detection ideal for unsupervised analysis.
	•	
Since real ECG datasets (e.g., MIT-BIH) require external access, I’ll generate a synthetic ECG signal using a standard model (e.g., McSharry et al.’s dynamic model) for portability. 

